msgid "Finite I2S2 slave TX on STM32F407"
msgstr "Finite I2S2 slave TX on STM32F407"

msgid "Use this exact baremetal role to transmit one caller-owned stereo16 frame block from an STM32F407VET6 or STM32F407ZGT6 under an independently controlled external I2S master. One task owns the transmitter, the external-clock handshake and failure drain. The implementation supplies finite normal DMA and explicit final access; the product supplies samples, rate, codec, master and recovery policy. Physical HIL is `not_executed`. IO-41 remains `in_progress`; continuous audio, SAI and PDM remain open."
msgstr "Use this exact baremetal role to transmit one caller-owned stereo16 frame block from an STM32F407VET6 or STM32F407ZGT6 under an independently controlled external I2S master. One task owns the transmitter, the external-clock handshake and failure drain. The implementation supplies finite normal DMA and explicit final access; the product supplies samples, rate, codec, master and recovery policy. Physical HIL is `not_executed`. IO-41 remains `in_progress`; continuous audio, SAI and PDM remain open."

msgid "Select one physical role"
msgstr "Select one physical role"

msgid "The authored role is `[i2s2]` with `profile = \"slave-tx-stereo16-pb12-pb13-pb15\"`. It resolves through the same validated hardware IR and resource plan as other controllers. A selected SPI2 personality, pin, DMA stream or vector conflict is rejected before generation. Omitting the role leaves it unselected; it creates no audio owner or target."
msgstr "The authored role is `[i2s2]` with `profile = \"slave-tx-stereo16-pb12-pb13-pb15\"`. It resolves through the same validated hardware IR and resource plan as other controllers. A selected SPI2 personality, pin, DMA stream or vector conflict is rejected before generation. Omitting the role leaves it unselected; it creates no audio owner or target."

