msgstr "Block size"

msgid "4..131068 B, divisible by four; 2..65534 DMA halfwords"
msgstr "4..131068 B, divisible by four; 2..65534 DMA halfwords"

msgid "DMA memory"
msgstr "DMA memory"

msgid "Entire aligned source span in main SRAM `[0x20000000, 0x20020000)`; CCM is excluded"
msgstr "Entire aligned source span in main SRAM `[0x20000000, 0x20020000)`; CCM is excluded"

msgid "For this stereo16 I2S format, `nx_frame_layout_audio` describes successive audio frames as rows. Keep that canonical layout: a multi-frame block may have multiple contiguous rows. The provider checks nonempty rows, `stride == row_bytes` and a bounded `rows * row_bytes == layout.bytes`, then takes a view covering the actual row geometry. The DMA count and settlement cover the complete block; there is no per-row loan or completion."
msgstr "For this stereo16 I2S format, `nx_frame_layout_audio` describes successive audio frames as rows. Keep that canonical layout: a multi-frame block may have multiple contiguous rows. The provider checks nonempty rows, `stride == row_bytes` and a bounded `rows * row_bytes == layout.bytes`, then takes a view covering the actual row geometry. The DMA count and settlement cover the complete block; there is no per-row loan or completion."

msgid "`nx_frame_layout_t` records storage geometry; it does not configure the wire or validate audio format metadata. The caller still supplies the declared little-endian stereo16 samples. Other audio-layout helper formats do not become supported transmitter formats."
msgstr "`nx_frame_layout_t` records storage geometry; it does not configure the wire or validate audio format metadata. The caller still supplies the declared little-endian stereo16 samples. Other audio-layout helper formats do not become supported transmitter formats."

msgid "The maintained VE input is below. The [ZG input](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/configure/assemblies/qiming-i2s2-slave-tx.toml) selects the corresponding exact Board package with the same role."
msgstr "The maintained VE input is below. The [ZG input](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/configure/assemblies/qiming-i2s2-slave-tx.toml) selects the corresponding exact Board package with the same role."

msgid "The component target is `Nexus::F407I2S2SlaveTx`, defined by [its CMake file](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/f407_i2s2_slave_tx/CMakeLists.txt) only for the validated selection. A consumer explicitly links it and constructs one stable readonly face with shared operations and separate zero-initialized owner storage. Factory lookup does not create or start an audio owner. The firmware owner storage is 88 B, excluding caller-owned request, stream, frame and payload storage. No task, allocation, queue or replay worker is created."
msgstr "The component target is `Nexus::F407I2S2SlaveTx`, defined by [its CMake file](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/f407_i2s2_slave_tx/CMakeLists.txt) only for the validated selection. A consumer explicitly links it and constructs one stable readonly face with shared operations and separate zero-initialized owner storage. Factory lookup does not create or start an audio owner. The firmware owner storage is 88 B, excluding caller-owned request, stream, frame and payload storage. No task, allocation, queue or replay worker is created."

msgid "The role uses external CK/WS; it does not enable PLLI2S or generate an audio clock. Chip AF capability does not establish a PCB route. The assembly supplies the exact part/package identity: device-group and Flash-density reads cannot authenticate an F407 or distinguish its physical package. The caller must meet DS8626 voltage, I/O, load and CK/WS/SD timing requirements and provide adequate DMA refill margin. This software defines no measured external-clock rate or additional characterized PCLK-to-CK ratio."
msgstr "The role uses external CK/WS; it does not enable PLLI2S or generate an audio clock. Chip AF capability does not establish a PCB route. The assembly supplies the exact part/package identity: device-group and Flash-density reads cannot authenticate an F407 or distinguish its physical package. The caller must meet DS8626 voltage, I/O, load and CK/WS/SD timing requirements and provide adequate DMA refill margin. This software defines no measured external-clock rate or additional characterized PCLK-to-CK ratio."

msgid "Keep Platform and transmitter ownership separate"
msgstr "Keep Platform and transmitter ownership separate"

msgid "The selected normal Platform startup assumes cold reset with no foreign running peripheral or bus master. It establishes the fixed clock and TIM2 epoch and holds GPIOB/DMA1 gates for the Platform lifetime. Clock-gating does not prove that a retained DMA engine is reset; attachment to unknown gated or running HAL state is unsupported."
msgstr "The selected normal Platform startup assumes cold reset with no foreign running peripheral or bus master. It establishes the fixed clock and TIM2 epoch and holds GPIOB/DMA1 gates for the Platform lifetime. Clock-gating does not prove that a retained DMA engine is reset; attachment to unknown gated or running HAL state is unsupported."

msgid "Transmitter initialization requires both shared gates already on. It owns the SPI2 gate, the SPI2/I2S2 personality, its selected pad fields and both vectors until successful transmitter stop. It never opens or withdraws GPIOB/DMA1 gates, resets the whole DMA controller or changes neighboring stream/pin state. Platform tracks its attempted gate additions before writes, preserves preexisting gates and retains cleanup responsibility if rollback fails."
msgstr "Transmitter initialization requires both shared gates already on. It owns the SPI2 gate, the SPI2/I2S2 personality, its selected pad fields and both vectors until successful transmitter stop. It never opens or withdraws GPIOB/DMA1 gates, resets the whole DMA controller or changes neighboring stream/pin state. Platform tracks its attempted gate additions before writes, preserves preexisting gates and retains cleanup responsibility if rollback fails."

msgid "One privileged unmasked task serializes initialization and every method. Concurrent Platform stop, reset/reclock/debugger writers and competing DMA, vector or pin owners are excluded. Failed calls do not authorize storage reuse. Stop and join the transmitter and every other shared-domain user, including external HAL users, before Platform stop withdraws its added gates or ends the TIM2 epoch. Old deadlines cannot cross Platform stop/restart."
msgstr "One privileged unmasked task serializes initialization and every method. Concurrent Platform stop, reset/reclock/debugger writers and competing DMA, vector or pin owners are excluded. Failed calls do not authorize storage reuse. Stop and join the transmitter and every other shared-domain user, including external HAL users, before Platform stop withdraws its added gates or ends the TIM2 epoch. Old deadlines cannot cross Platform stop/restart."

msgid "Accept the frame before arming the master"
msgstr "Accept the frame before arming the master"

msgid "![FIG-30: exact finite I2S2 ownership, arm handshake and final-access proof](../assets/diagrams/f407-i2s2-slave-tx.svg)"
msgstr "![FIG-30: exact finite I2S2 ownership, arm handshake and final-access proof](../assets/diagrams/f407-i2s2-slave-tx.svg)"

msgid "FIG-30: exact finite I2S2 ownership, arm handshake and final-access proof"
msgstr "FIG-30: exact finite I2S2 ownership, arm handshake and final-access proof"

msgid "**FIG-30 is a reference lifecycle for this exact role.** Solid arrows show required order or a named branch; dashed arrows show retained responsibility and bounded retry. It is based on the public header, provider and selected System implementation linked below. It establishes neither physical clock silence nor hardware qualification."
msgstr "**FIG-30 is a reference lifecycle for this exact role.** Solid arrows show required order or a named branch; dashed arrows show retained responsibility and bounded retry. It is based on the public header, provider and selected System implementation linked below. It establishes neither physical clock silence nor hardware qualification."

msgid "Hold CK continuously LOW and WS HIGH before initialization and submission, and keep them there until acquire-observed ACTIVE. Register pin reads sample instants; the caller's master coordination establishes the continuous quiet interval. Each normal restart begins with the left channel."
msgstr "Hold CK continuously LOW and WS HIGH before initialization and submission, and keep them there until acquire-observed ACTIVE. Register pin reads sample instants; the caller's master coordination establishes the continuous quiet interval. Each normal restart begins with the left channel."

msgid "Start Platform successfully, then initialize fresh transmitter storage with the stable face and a positive `poll_limit`. Initialization can retain cleanup responsibility on IO; keep its storage live and call stop."
msgstr "Start Platform successfully, then initialize fresh transmitter storage with the stable face and a positive `poll_limit`. Initialization can retain cleanup responsibility on IO; keep its storage live and call stop."

msgid "Build the complete contiguous frame with the ordinary stream/frame helpers and acquire its original `nx_frame_dma_loan_t`. Initialize and prepare the request with an absolute deadline in the current live TIM2 epoch, and assign that loan to its `source`. Controls must be correctly aligned, live and disjoint from every full-capacity pool slot, including unused payload tails."
msgstr "Build the complete contiguous frame with the ordinary stream/frame helpers and acquire its original `nx_frame_dma_loan_t`. Initialize and prepare the request with an absolute deadline in the current live TIM2 epoch, and assign that loan to its `source`. Controls must be correctly aligned, live and disjoint from every full-capacity pool slot, including unused payload tails."

msgid "Submit through the face. Rejection retains no request or frame reference and introduces no submission hardware effect. `NX_SUCCESS` means ACCEPTED: the exact whole-frame loan and request are borrowed. The provider publishes QUEUED before the first read-clear SR observation or possible DMA prefetch. Initialization separately owns cleanup before its SR reads."
msgstr "Submit through the face. Rejection retains no request or frame reference and introduces no submission hardware effect. `NX_SUCCESS` means ACCEPTED: the exact whole-frame loan and request are borrowed. The provider publishes QUEUED before the first read-clear SR observation or possible DMA prefetch. Initialization separately owns cleanup before its SR reads."

msgid "Submission runs bounded arming synchronously. It programs the full halfword count, enables DMA, then TXDMAEN, then I2SE. ACTIVE requires observed I2SE enable, one prefetched DR halfword (`NDTR = N - 1`, `TXE = 0`) and at least three actual 1 MHz TIM2 ticks after enable readback. `BSY = 0` is not an arm prerequisite. A CPU polling count is not elapsed time. The return state may already be ACTIVE or DRAINING; QUEUED and ACCEPTED alone never authorize CK."
msgstr "Submission runs bounded arming synchronously. It programs the full halfword count, enables DMA, then TXDMAEN, then I2SE. ACTIVE requires observed I2SE enable, one prefetched DR halfword (`NDTR = N - 1`, `TXE = 0`) and at least three actual 1 MHz TIM2 ticks after enable readback. `BSY = 0` is not an arm prerequisite. A CPU polling count is not elapsed time. The return state may already be ACTIVE or DRAINING; QUEUED and ACCEPTED alone never authorize CK."

msgid "Only acquire-observed ACTIVE authorizes the master to clock the declared complete stereo frames. The master must stop before requesting a missing next word. The same task calls `service` to observe completion, errors and deadline expiry and to progress drain. No provider IRQ advances the request."
msgstr "Only acquire-observed ACTIVE authorizes the master to clock the declared complete stereo frames. The master must stop before requesting a missing next word. The same task calls `service` to observe completion, errors and deadline expiry and to progress drain. No provider IRQ advances the request."

msgid "An SR read clears UDR/FRE, so each request-path observation occurs after acceptance and preserves any fault as the first operation error. A later clean read or late DMA completion cannot turn that error into success. The absolute deadline covers the whole operation, including wire and final address/vector withdrawal. Arming observation-budget exhaustion can also produce TIMEOUT; it does not prove that a particular duration elapsed. `poll_limit` bounds each observation loop and never guarantees progress by an external master."
msgstr "An SR read clears UDR/FRE, so each request-path observation occurs after acceptance and preserves any fault as the first operation error. A later clean read or late DMA completion cannot turn that error into success. The absolute deadline covers the whole operation, including wire and final address/vector withdrawal. Arming observation-budget exhaustion can also produce TIMEOUT; it does not prove that a particular duration elapsed. `poll_limit` bounds each observation loop and never guarantees progress by an external master."

msgid "Prove final access before releasing storage"
msgstr "Prove final access before releasing storage"

msgid "Observation or stage"
msgstr "Observation or stage"

msgid "Required action and remaining responsibility"
msgstr "Required action and remaining responsibility"

msgid "Normal `TCIF` and `NDTR = 0`"
msgstr "Normal `TCIF` and `NDTR = 0`"

msgid "Memory-count completion only. Keep the request and frame borrowed. Software DMA disable can also set TCIF with a nonzero count."
msgstr "Memory-count completion only. Keep the request and frame borrowed. Software DMA disable can also set TCIF with a nonzero count."

msgid "Cancel, timeout or failure"
msgstr "Cancel, timeout or failure"

msgid "Preserve the first error and enter DRAINING; every error/cancellation reports zero transferred bytes."
msgstr "Preserve the first error and enter DRAINING; every error/cancellation reports zero transferred bytes."

msgid "Engine withdrawal"
msgstr "Engine withdrawal"

msgid "Clear TXDMAEN and DMA EN with readback before relying on serializer drain. A failed clear retains the borrow."
msgstr "Clear TXDMAEN and DMA EN with readback before relying on serializer drain. A failed clear retains the borrow."

msgid "Any I2SE enable attempt"
msgstr "Any I2SE enable attempt"

msgid "Observe `TXE = 1`, then a separate fresh `BSY = 0`, before clearing I2SE with readback. An ignored enable write is still an attempted enable."
msgstr "Observe `TXE = 1`, then a separate fresh `BSY = 0`, before clearing I2SE with readback. An ignored enable write is still an attempted enable."

msgid "No I2SE attempt"
msgstr "No I2SE attempt"

msgid "An accepted early setup failure may prove engine and reference withdrawal without waiting for serializer flags."
msgstr "An accepted early setup failure may prove engine and reference withdrawal without waiting for serializer flags."

msgid "Serializer already proved quiet"
msgstr "Serializer already proved quiet"

msgid "Preserve that proof across later cleanup retries; do not demand TXE again from disabled I2S."
msgstr "Preserve that proof across later cleanup retries; do not demand TXE again from disabled I2S."

msgid "Reference withdrawal"
msgstr "Reference withdrawal"

msgid "Clear stream configuration, addresses/count and flags; withdraw and prove disabled, not pending and inactive vectors."
msgstr "Clear stream configuration, addresses/count and flags; withdraw and prove disabled, not pending and inactive vectors."

msgid "Every proof joined"
msgstr "Every proof joined"

msgid "Detach provider references, release the original whole-frame loan, then release-publish SETTLED as the final request access."
msgstr "Detach provider references, release the original whole-frame loan, then release-publish SETTLED as the final request access."

msgid "Missing proof"
msgstr "Missing proof"

msgid "Retain QUARANTINED storage. A drain-loop bound can return BUSY; timeout, TC or a zero DMA count never substitutes for final access."
msgstr "Retain QUARANTINED storage. A drain-loop bound can return BUSY; timeout, TC or a zero DMA count never substitutes for final access."

msgid "Acquire-observe SETTLED before reading the terminal result or reusing the request and frame storage. Successful completion reports the full submitted byte count. Error and cancellation report zero; a DMA count cannot establish serialized audio bytes. Join external observers before their own storage is reused. While stop has not closed admission, successful request settlement keeps the initialized transmitter ready for another separately prepared block; it does not release its physical role."
msgstr "Acquire-observe SETTLED before reading the terminal result or reusing the request and frame storage. Successful completion reports the full submitted byte count. Error and cancellation report zero; a DMA count cannot establish serialized audio bytes. Join external observers before their own storage is reused. While stop has not closed admission, successful request settlement keeps the initialized transmitter ready for another separately prepared block; it does not release its physical role."

msgid "With CK idle after prefill, DR cannot empty. Cancellation therefore retains the loan until the product coordinates enough drain clocks for the actual TXE and fresh BSY proof. This error drain may underrun or produce partial/invalid audio; it does not promise a complete stereo frame. Keep the first failure and restart later only at the left channel. Continuing `service` or `stop` through the same owner can retry a stalled-clock cleanup while its hardware/time history remains known."
msgstr "With CK idle after prefill, DR cannot empty. Cancellation therefore retains the loan until the product coordinates enough drain clocks for the actual TXE and fresh BSY proof. This error drain may underrun or produce partial/invalid audio; it does not promise a complete stereo frame. Keep the first failure and restart later only at the left channel. Continuing `service` or `stop` through the same owner can retry a stalled-clock cleanup while its hardware/time history remains known."

msgid "Observed reset, shared-gate/clock-profile loss or invalid time history while borrowed permanently quarantines this instance and its loan. Restoring reset-looking registers cannot establish prior final access. There is no reset or recovery API that revokes that borrow. A product owns the response to an unrecoverable controller/master failure."
msgstr "Observed reset, shared-gate/clock-profile loss or invalid time history while borrowed permanently quarantines this instance and its loan. Restoring reset-looking registers cannot establish prior final access. There is no reset or recovery API that revokes that borrow. A product owns the response to an unrecoverable controller/master failure."

msgid "`stop` closes admission and requests cancellation. Repeat it after service has proved any outstanding cleanup. Only successful transmitter stop returns the selected pads/SPI2 personality and SPI2 gate; shared GPIOB/DMA1 gates remain for Platform users. Failed stop retains every unfinished borrow and owned effect."
msgstr "`stop` closes admission and requests cancellation. Repeat it after service has proved any outstanding cleanup. Only successful transmitter stop returns the selected pads/SPI2 personality and SPI2 gate; shared GPIOB/DMA1 gates remain for Platform users. Failed stop retains every unfinished borrow and owned effect."

msgid "Assess the current evidence"
msgstr "Assess the current evidence"

msgid "Normal ARM builds passed for the selected VE and ZG I2S2 configurations and the omitted default. Scoped Native and selection tests, SDK/release checks, retention checks and both corrected caller-face audits also passed. One relocated, nonpublishable development Source SDK passed export, rename, verification, a public C11 consumer link, the selected-image audit and reverification; this covered one VE image. The [source-bound evidence](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/testing/evidence/f407-i2s2-20261020/README.md) records full-image resources rather than isolated driver cost. This is partial development evidence: it does not qualify the full v10 matrix, clean main, formal/OCI delivery or physical HIL. The API and full-site build receipts and the final commit gate must be assessed separately. Original strict Wshadow and harness-setup failures are retained separately from functional TDD."
msgstr "Normal ARM builds passed for the selected VE and ZG I2S2 configurations and the omitted default. Scoped Native and selection tests, SDK/release checks, retention checks and both corrected caller-face audits also passed. One relocated, nonpublishable development Source SDK passed export, rename, verification, a public C11 consumer link, the selected-image audit and reverification; this covered one VE image. The [source-bound evidence](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/testing/evidence/f407-i2s2-20261020/README.md) records full-image resources rather than isolated driver cost. This is partial development evidence: it does not qualify the full v10 matrix, clean main, formal/OCI delivery or physical HIL. The API and full-site build receipts and the final commit gate must be assessed separately. Original strict Wshadow and harness-setup failures are retained separately from functional TDD."

msgid "The normal public-consumer source is [f407-i2s2-slave-tx.c](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/cmake/package/verification/io_evolution/consumers/f407-i2s2-slave-tx.c). It links public construction and whole-frame ownership paths; linking does not execute those calls. It is not an external clock source or a completed hardware tutorial. No physical execution or valid audio result is claimed. Continuous DBM, gapless replay, SAI/PDM, other formats/pads/parts/backends and physical HIL remain open under IO-41."
msgstr "The normal public-consumer source is [f407-i2s2-slave-tx.c](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/cmake/package/verification/io_evolution/consumers/f407-i2s2-slave-tx.c). It links public construction and whole-frame ownership paths; linking does not execute those calls. It is not an external clock source or a completed hardware tutorial. No physical execution or valid audio result is claimed. Continuous DBM, gapless replay, SAI/PDM, other formats/pads/parts/backends and physical HIL remain open under IO-41."

msgid "The hardware sequence follows RM0090 Rev22 sections 28.4.6–28.4.8 and 10.3.13–10.3.14, with DS8626 electrical requirements and the pinned ES0182 scope. The SPI-only BSY erratum workaround is not substituted for the I2S shutdown sequence. Source identities are maintained in [the F407 reference manifest](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/soc/stm32f407/references.json)."
msgstr "The hardware sequence follows RM0090 Rev22 sections 28.4.6–28.4.8 and 10.3.13–10.3.14, with DS8626 electrical requirements and the pinned ES0182 scope. The SPI-only BSY erratum workaround is not substituted for the I2S shutdown sequence. Source identities are maintained in [the F407 reference manifest](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/soc/stm32f407/references.json)."

